Constants:
    RECORDER_SAMPLERATE: Frequency (HZ) of AudioRecord sampling
    RECORDER_SAMPLE_DURATION_MS: Duration of audio clip processed

    RECORDER_CHANNELS: How many channels are encoded by AudioRecord
        Recommendation: Unless multiple channels are required, this should be left as-is.
    RECORDER_AUDIO_ENCODING: How many bits are used and what format is used to encode incoming audio
        Recommendation: If you need to change this,
            I will need to refactor AudioCollector and AudioProcessor
            to support the new size of each sample.

    PERMISSIONS_REQUEST_ALL: Arbitrary value used to track what permissions request was received.


YourClass:
    Example Class, designed to be simple to implement your processing code within / over.


MainActivity:
    The primary class in the application. Manages the UI, Permissions and Location Service.

    AudioTrack was implemented for testing purposes. The `Play` button plays back the most recent batch of recorded audio.

    Wire-up from the UI to AudioCollector is not required; AudioCollector can be set to automatically begin in `configure`.

    Permissions:
        RECORD_AUDIO: Required to record audio.
        INTERNET: Required to send data to Firebase.
        ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION: Required for precise location services.
            ACCESS_COURSE_LOCATION can be used in case high precision is not desired.

    onCreate:
        called when the app is opened. Any initial setup of services (Firebase, Location, etc) should belong here

    onStart:
        Called when the app becomes visible. This is between onCreate and when the user can interact with the app.
        Should setup anything after onCreate that is not restricted by permissions.

    checkPermissions:
        Called during onCreate to check all required permissions.

    onRequestPermissionsResult:
        Called once the user has accepted/denied all requests for permissions.
        If Setup / User Interaction / Standard Operation depends on permissions, it should go into configure().

    configure:
        Called to setup anything that is restricted by permissions.
        Location Services and Audio are the primary items.

    checkEnableButtons:
        Runs once.
        Enables usage of Start / Stop buttons.

    setButtonHandlers:
        Wires up UI Buttons to the appropriate actions in btnClick.

    updateUI:
        Updates the UI with the most recent processing result.
        Called by AudioProcessor.

    getLocation:
        Returns the most recently updated location.

    onLocationChanged, onProviderDisabled, onProviderEnabled, onStatusChanged:
        Logging functions for the Location Service.
        `onLocationChanged` sets the location to be sent to Firebase.


AudioCollector:
    recording_ms: See Constants.
    sample_rate: See Constants

    listener:
        Every ~recording_ms, reads the last recording_ms worth of samples into a buffer,
            and starts a thread to process it.

    startRecording:
        creates a new AudioRecord and begins listening to the microphone.

    stopRecording:
        stops the AudioRecord from recording.

    isRecording:
        whether startRecording or stopRecording was last called. Default: false.

    getRecordingMs, getSampleRate, getSamplesPerProcessingBuffer:
        Returns the appropriate internal variable.

    setRecordingMs, setSampleRate:
        Sets the appropriate variable, and restarts the AudioRecord.

    getLastRecording:
        Returns the most recent AudioRecord buffer.


AudioProcessor:
    buffer: recording_ms long buffer of sound audio from AudioCollector.
    sample_rate: See Constants.

    run:
        Collects the following information:
            Timestamp: Current Time
            Location: Current Location provided by Location Services
            Audio_Blob: Base 64 encoded audio data from buffer
            Is_Gunshot: Whether or not YourClass says the audio contains a gunshot
            Sample_Rate: See Constants

        Uses the FirebaseFirestore API to put the above in a document
            in the processedAudio collection.

        RECOMMENDATION:
            Once you no longer require testing for false negatives, only send requests to Firebase when a gunshot is detected.
            That way, you will stay under the Free-Tier write limit (20k/day)


GunshotDocument:
    Contains the information described above in `AudioProcessor.run`


Utils:
    short_to_byte:
        Helper function for preparing audio data for Base 64 encoding
        Note: Low byte is encoded first